# agent worktrees
.claude/

# Where the desktop app drops files delivered into the chat. It lands inside the checkout, and
# one untracked folder is enough to make `git status --porcelain` non-empty -- which sends
# sync-history.ps1 down its "the tree is dirty, so the files may already be here" path, where it
# stages everything and compares it against the incoming history. The comparison then fails on
# every file the incoming commits touch and prints a 32-file diff that looks like data loss and
# is nothing of the kind. Ignoring the folder keeps the tree clean so git just fast-forwards.
Claude outputs/

# the Harmony scanner, built for a release by scripts/sidecar.mjs
src-tauri/binaries/
